 <p>
  It has been flying for a little over a hundred years.
</p>

<p>
  In the beginning, it could not travel very far.<br />
  Its body was heavy, and the time it could remain in the sky was short.<br />
  People kept changing its body,<br />
  making it a little lighter, a little faster,<br />
  able to travel a little farther.
</p>

<p>
  With time, it moved farther and farther away<br />
  from the place where it was born.
</p>

<p>
  It heard languages it had never heard before<br />
  and carried faces it had never seen.
</p>

<p>
  People packed their belongings into small bags and climbed aboard.<br />
  Some came back.<br />
  Some never did.
</p>

<p>
  They carried clothes, food, and books.<br />
  They carried songs and ideas.<br />
  Sometimes they left them somewhere else before returning.
</p>

<p>
  So many things passed through its body.
</p>

<p>
  The landscape below kept changing too.
</p>

<p>
  Cities grew larger, and nights became brighter.<br />
  People built things higher and higher<br />
  and learned how to fit more and more into smaller things.
</p>

<p>
  What they called beautiful kept changing.<br />
  So did what they believed was right.
</p>

<p>
  And yet, strangely,<br />
  some things kept returning.
</p>

<p>
  On certain days, it could no longer cross the sky<br />
  it had crossed every day.
</p>

<p>
  Borders closed.<br />
  Lights disappeared.<br />
  Black smoke rose in the distance.
</p>

<p>
  People sometimes destroyed in a very short time<br />
  what had taken them years to build.
</p>

<p>
  When it was over,<br />
  they began building again.
</p>

<p>
  They raised things so they could remember.<br />
  They said they would not forget.
</p>

<p>
  It has seen this many times.
</p>

<p>
  And when enough time passes,<br />
  there is always another part of the sky<br />
  that can no longer be crossed.
</p>

<p>
  Each time, it changes direction.
</p>

<p>
  There are no roads visible in the sky,<br />
  but it has routes it travels every day.
</p>

<p>
  A place that could be reached yesterday<br />
  has to be flown around today.
</p>

<p>
  It no longer finds this strange.
</p>

<p>
  After flying for a little over a hundred years,<br />
  one gets used to roads disappearing<br />
  and appearing again.
</p>

<p>
  People keep moving.
</p>

<p>
  Objects, languages, music, and ideas<br />
  move with them.
</p>

<p>
  It carries them<br />
  and rises into the sky again.
</p>

<p>
  Below, something is being built.
</p>

<p>
  And somewhere else,<br />
  something already built<br />
  is disappearing.
</p>

<p>
  It keeps flying.
</p>

